## Screens and components annotated

48 hinted elements across 9 files (all `src/components/ui/*` shadcn primitives left untouched — they already spread `{...props}`, so **no component widening was needed**).

| Screen | What was hinted |
|---|---|
| Main — header/toolbar | `fields.config.open`, `app.toolbar` region, `search.query` + `search.clear`, `view.sort` select, `view.mode.table`/`.card` toggles, `entry.add` |
| Main — table view | `entries.table` collection on `TableBody`, `entries.table.columns` collection on the header row |
| Main — card view | `entries.grid` collection, per-card title/values/controls |
| Main — status bar | `entries.count`, `view.sort.summary` observables |
| Entry dialog | `entry.dialog` region, `entry.dialog.title`, `entry.dialog.form` collection, cancel/save |
| Field config dialog | `fields.dialog` region, `fields.list` collection, `fields.add` region + name/type/submit |
| 404 | `notfound` region, message, `notfound.home` → `home.page` |

**Id namespaces:** `entries.*` (region → `entries.table` / `entries.grid` collections), `entry.*` (add button + dialog), `fields.*` (config dialog + list), `view.*` (mode, sort), `search.*`, `notfound.*`. State keys: `search.query`, `view.mode`, `view.sort`, `entries.count`, `entry.<fieldId>`, `field.name`/`field.type`/`field.new.*`.

## Validation

- **Skill linter: 0 errors, 0 warnings.** The 2 `info` items are flat ids on top-level regions (`entries`, `notfound`), which the linter itself calls fine for a top-level region.
- **What the linter can't see**, I checked at runtime with Playwright across all five screens: **zero duplicate ids** on any screen, and **zero orphan `.item.` ids** — every collection container is a genuine DOM ancestor of its items. All five collections fold: `entries.table` (35 elements → 5 keys), `entries.grid` (35 → 5), `fields.list` (12 → 4), `entries.table.columns` (4 → 4), `entry.dialog.form` (4 → 4). `data-semtag-options` strings match the rendered menus exactly, since both are built from the same source.
- **Project checks:** `tsc --noEmit` clean, `vite build` succeeds, no console/page errors. `npm run lint` reports 3 errors + 7 warnings, but **all pre-existing** — they're in `ui/command.tsx`, `ui/textarea.tsx` and `tailwind.config.ts`, which I verified are byte-identical to the pristine copy. I diffed my 9 files against pristine: every non-semtag line is tag reformatting with classNames/handlers preserved verbatim, plus two derived constants (`titleField`, `fieldTypeOptions`).

## Judgement calls worth flagging

- **The one thing that won't fold:** the per-field type-select options (`fields.list.item.field-2.type.option.*`) carry `.item.` in their id but Radix portals them to `document.body`, outside the `fields.list` container. Renaming them would break the spec's `<trigger-id>.option.<value>` convention, so I kept the spec shape. Cost is bounded: 4 elements, only while a menu is open.
- **Table checkbox cells render an icon with no text**, so the extractor captures no value for them. I did not fabricate a literal — the same data is readable in card view, which renders "Yes"/"No" badges.
- **ViewToggle active state** isn't readable as text, so per §5 form 2 the active button gets `view.mode,selected`. This is the only place I encoded a literal state value.
- **Deliberately unhinted:** decorative icons, the "No entries found" empty states (`entries.count` already reports 0), the static "Drag entries to reorder" hint (tagging it would have duplicated `view.sort.summary`), and `FieldConfigDialog`'s fallback trigger button, which is dead code since `Index` always passes a trigger.

I left `node_modules/` in place (gitignored) since I had to install it to run the checks; `dist/` and all temp scripts were removed.

